Key dependencies (these blocks must run first or in order):
1. B6 (K8s env) must precede any nexi↔xnch integration tests
2. B2 must precede anything that depends on episodes existing (M1, M7)
3. M1 (canonical store decision) must precede M4, M5, M7 — these are all downstream of that decision
So the optimal execution order is:
1. Phase 0 (blockers): kubernetes-specialist + debugger — in parallel, no deps between them
2. Phase 1 (design decision): database-architect — decide canonical store architecture
3. Phase 2 (parallel after decisions): api-architect + refactoring-specialist + llm-architect + microservices-architect

